filename: Ocampo2025-Table2.csv
material: Fused Silica
formula: SiO2
material_info:
- High-purity fused silica samples (Corning 7980 HPFS 0F Grade, 800-1100 ppm H2O).
rho_ref: 2.200
rho_ref_std: 0.004
rho_ref_units: g/cm^3
bibkey: Ocampo2025
bibtex: "@article{Ocampo2025, author = {L. K. Ocampo and J. M. Winey and T. S. Duffy}, doi = {10.1029/2025JB031366}, journal = {Journal of Geophysical Research: Solid Earth}, pages = {e2025JB031366}, title = {Sound velocity and Grüneisen parameter in shock-melted silica at deep Earth pressures}, volume = {130}, year = {2025}}"
platform: Two-stage light gas gun at the Institute for Shock Physics at Washington State University.
methods:
- Plate-impact experiments using either a Release Wave Overtake (RWO) or a wave transmission configuration.
- The impactor was either OFE C101 copper or platinum.
- A Monte Carlo approach was used to propagate uncertainties in the measured quantities.
calibration:
- The Hugoniot states were determined using standard impedance matching methods at the impact surface.
- The impactor Hugoniot equations of state for copper and platinum were used as standards.
- Wave profiles were corrected for shock-induced changes in the refractive index of the [100] LiF window.
actions:
- Gemini
- create
- 2025-09-08
- Extracted experimental data from wave profile measurements for RWO and transmission experiments from Table 2.
exp_type:
- single-shock
- PV
- sound-speed
diagnostics:
- VISAR (Velocity Interferometer System for Any Reflector)
- PDV (Photon Doppler Velocimetry)
primary_data:
- uflyer
- us
- up_window
